<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bourtzi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1471</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Castello dello Scoglio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bourtzi is a small castle on an islet in the harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nafplio</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, built by the Venetians in 1471 to guard the entrance to the port, which could be closed with a chain. Later held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and again by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, it was used in modern times as a residence for executioners and as a hotel, and is now a landmark of the town.</p></div>
